  "notes": [
    "Dates are 'YYYY-MM'. A variant matches when built_from <= build date < built_before.",
    "Registration date is used in place of build date, so a car built just before August 1985 but registered after it can match the wrong variant.",
    "A variant lists every fuel and ignition chapter its engines might use, because owners rarely know their fuel system. chapters_by_engine_code narrows this when the engine code is known.",
    "Chapters 2B, 2D, 4C, 4D and 4F only add to a parent chapter (2A, 2C or 4B), so the parent chapter is included as well.",
    "Intervals are 'whichever comes first' when both miles and months are given; null means the manual gives no limit of that kind.",
    "Weekly checks (every 250 miles or weekly) are in the manual's 'Weekly checks' pages, not in these schedules.",
    "Post-August 1985: engine oil and brake pads are every 12 months, or every 10 000 miles if the car covers more than 10 000 miles a year.",
    "The post-August 1985 timing belt interval is printed as '40 000 miles (160 000 km)'; the km figure is a misprint, 40 000 miles is used.",
    "Trims are only those the manual names. Add other trims (for example Driver or Carat) from a separate source."
  ]
